Two sorted arrays nums1 and nums2 of different sizes, find the median of the two sorted arrays.
Your solution must have a time complexity of O(log(m+n)) or better.

CODE : 
# Take first sorted array as input and convert strings into integers
nums1 = list(map(int, input().split()))
# Take second sorted array as input and convert strings into integers
nums2 = list(map(int, input().split()))
# Combine both arrays and sort all elements in ascending order
arr = sorted(nums1 + nums2)
# Find the total number of elements in the combined array
n = len(arr)
# Check whether the total number of elements is even
if n % 2 == 0:
    # If even, take the two middle elements and calculate their average
    median = (arr[n//2 - 1] + arr[n//2]) / 2
else:
    # If odd, the middle element itself is the median
    median = arr[n//2]
# Print the calculated median
print(median)

Input1:
1 3
2

Output1:
2

Input2:
1 3
2 4

Output2:
2.5

Input3:
